---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Ui.astro';
---

<Base title="Forms">
  <h1>Forms</h1>
  <p>
    Filled newsprint slots with a printed rule: a 1px tan hairline box whose
    bottom rule is 2px ink — the line you type on. Labels speak in the
    typewriter voice, placeholders in Goudy italic. Checkboxes stamp an ink
    X, the radio is the one round control, and the switch is a stage lever.
  </p>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>TEXT INPUT</h2>
    <p>Typewriter label above the slot, optional help beneath — all inside a <code>.mk-field</code>.</p>
    <div class="field-demo">
      <div class="mk-field">
        <label for="d-act">Name of the act</label>
        <input class="mk-input" id="d-act" type="text" placeholder="e.g. The Amazing Flannel Brothers" />
        <p class="mk-field__help">As it will be printed on the bill.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;div class="mk-field"&gt;
  &lt;label for="act"&gt;Name of the act&lt;/label&gt;
  &lt;input class="mk-input" id="act" type="text"
         placeholder="e.g. The Amazing Flannel Brothers" /&gt;
  &lt;p class="mk-field__help"&gt;As it will be printed on the bill.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>SELECT</h2>
    <p>
      Native <code>&lt;select&gt;</code> with the chrome stripped; the caret
      is a small solid triangle drawn in CSS — a printed control, not an
      icon.
    </p>
    <div class="field-demo">
      <div class="mk-field">
        <label for="d-billing">Billing</label>
        <select class="mk-select" id="d-billing">
          <option>Top of the bill</option>
          <option>Second billing</option>
          <option>The chorus</option>
          <option>After the intermission</option>
        </select>
      </div>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;select class="mk-select" id="billing"&gt;
  &lt;option&gt;Top of the bill&lt;/option&gt;
  &lt;option&gt;Second billing&lt;/option&gt;
&lt;/select&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>TEXTAREA</h2>
    <p>A taller slot; resizes vertically only.</p>
    <div class="field-demo">
      <div class="mk-field">
        <label for="d-notes">Notes for the stage manager</label>
        <textarea class="mk-textarea" id="d-notes" placeholder="The pyrotechnics require a permit and a calmer host."></textarea>
      </div>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;textarea class="mk-textarea" id="notes"&gt;&lt;/textarea&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>CHECKBOX</h2>
    <p>
      A square 2px rule that takes a stamped ink X — it appears whole, like a
      rubber stamp. The <code>.mk-choice</code> row is the 44px tap target.
    </p>
    <div class="field-demo">
      <label class="mk-choice">
        <input class="mk-checkbox" type="checkbox" checked />
        <span>Reserve a box for the Taylors</span>
      </label>
      <label class="mk-choice">
        <input class="mk-checkbox" type="checkbox" />
        <span>Print in the Sunday edition</span>
      </label>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;label class="mk-choice"&gt;
  &lt;input class="mk-checkbox" type="checkbox" /&gt;
  &lt;span&gt;Reserve a box for the Taylors&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/label&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>RADIO GROUP</h2>
    <p>
      The one round control — a circle is geometry, not softness. Grouped in
      a <code>.mk-fieldset</code> whose legend speaks in the form-kicker
      voice.
    </p>
    <div class="field-demo">
      <fieldset class="mk-fieldset">
        <legend>Performance</legend>
        <label class="mk-choice">
          <input class="mk-radio" type="radio" name="d-perf" checked />
          <span>Evening</span>
        </label>
        <label class="mk-choice">
          <input class="mk-radio" type="radio" name="d-perf" />
          <span>Matinee</span>
        </label>
        <label class="mk-choice">
          <input class="mk-radio" type="radio" name="d-perf" />
          <span>Twice daily</span>
        </label>
      </fieldset>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;fieldset class="mk-fieldset"&gt;
  &lt;legend&gt;Performance&lt;/legend&gt;
  &lt;label class="mk-choice"&gt;
    &lt;input class="mk-radio" type="radio" name="perf" /&gt;
    &lt;span&gt;Evening&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;/label&gt;
&lt;/fieldset&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>SWITCH</h2>
    <p>
      A hard-edged stage lever: the ink block jumps to the far end in two
      stepped frames, and the rail goes ochre when ON — a sanctioned accent
      spot, because the ON state is information.
    </p>
    <div class="field-demo">
      <label class="mk-choice">
        <input class="mk-switch" type="checkbox" checked />
        <span>Footlights</span>
      </label>
      <label class="mk-choice">
        <input class="mk-switch" type="checkbox" />
        <span>Follow spot</span>
      </label>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;label class="mk-choice"&gt;
  &lt;input class="mk-switch" type="checkbox" /&gt;
  &lt;span&gt;Footlights&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/label&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>ERROR STATE</h2>
    <p>
      The rule turns ochre all the way around and the message speaks in
      character. The error doubles as this view&rsquo;s accent ration — a
      form with an error has no other ochre spot. Wire
      <code>aria-invalid</code> and <code>aria-describedby</code>.
    </p>
    <div class="field-demo">
      <div class="mk-field mk-field--error">
        <label for="d-venue">Venue</label>
        <input
          class="mk-input"
          id="d-venue"
          type="text"
          value="The Hardware Theatre, Detroit"
          aria-invalid="true"
          aria-describedby="d-venue-err"
        />
        <p class="mk-field__error" id="d-venue-err">That address is not on the bill.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;div class="mk-field mk-field--error"&gt;
  &lt;label for="venue"&gt;Venue&lt;/label&gt;
  &lt;input class="mk-input" id="venue" aria-invalid="true"
         aria-describedby="venue-err" /&gt;
  &lt;p class="mk-field__error" id="venue-err"&gt;That address is not on the bill.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>NOTHING WILL BE PRINTED HERE</h2>
    <p>
      Disabled slots go dashed on the bottom rule and the fill empties —
      the dashed line is the house vocabulary for absence, never an opacity
      wash.
    </p>
    <div class="field-demo">
      <div class="mk-field">
        <label for="d-closed">Box office</label>
        <input class="mk-input" id="d-closed" type="text" value="Closed for the season" disabled />
      </div>
      <label class="mk-choice">
        <input class="mk-checkbox" type="checkbox" disabled />
        <span style="color: var(--mk-color-disabled-text);">Standing room</span>
      </label>
      <label class="mk-choice">
        <input class="mk-switch" type="checkbox" disabled />
        <span style="color: var(--mk-color-disabled-text);">House lights</span>
      </label>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;input class="mk-input" value="Closed for the season" disabled /&gt;
&lt;input class="mk-checkbox" type="checkbox" disabled /&gt;
&lt;input class="mk-switch" type="checkbox" disabled /&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>THE BOOKING FORM</h2>
    <p>Everything together — labels, help, one error in character, and the action row.</p>
    <form class="form-demo" novalidate>
      <div class="mk-field">
        <label for="f-act">Name of the act</label>
        <input class="mk-input" id="f-act" type="text" value="Tim Taylor · More Power" />
      </div>

      <div class="mk-field">
        <label for="f-billing">Billing</label>
        <select class="mk-select" id="f-billing">
          <option>Top of the bill</option>
          <option>Second billing</option>
          <option>The chorus</option>
        </select>
      </div>

      <div class="mk-field mk-field--error">
        <label for="f-runtime">Running time</label>
        <input
          class="mk-input"
          id="f-runtime"
          type="text"
          value="ninety-one minutes"
          aria-invalid="true"
          aria-describedby="f-runtime-help f-runtime-err"
        />
        <p class="mk-field__help" id="f-runtime-help">In minutes, as a figure.</p>
        <p class="mk-field__error" id="f-runtime-err">The orchestra cannot count words.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="mk-field">
        <label for="f-notes">Notes for the stage manager</label>
        <textarea class="mk-textarea" id="f-notes" placeholder="Optional"></textarea>
      </div>

      <fieldset class="mk-fieldset">
        <legend>Performance</legend>
        <label class="mk-choice">
          <input class="mk-radio" type="radio" name="f-perf" checked />
          <span>Evening</span>
        </label>
        <label class="mk-choice">
          <input class="mk-radio" type="radio" name="f-perf" />
          <span>Matinee</span>
        </label>
        <label class="mk-choice">
          <input class="mk-radio" type="radio" name="f-perf" />
          <span>Twice daily</span>
        </label>
      </fieldset>

      <label class="mk-choice">
        <input class="mk-checkbox" type="checkbox" checked />
        <span>Reserve a box for the Taylors</span>
      </label>

      <div class="form-actions">
        <button class="mk-btn mk-btn--primary" type="submit">Book the act</button>
        <button class="mk-btn mk-btn--ghost" type="button">Hold the page</button>
      </div>
    </form>
  </section>

  <style>
    .field-demo {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: var(--mk-space-sm);
      max-width: 24rem;
    }

    .form-demo {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: var(--mk-space-lg);
      max-width: 24rem;
    }

    .form-actions {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: var(--mk-space-sm);
    }

    section.mk-card + section.mk-card {
      margin-top: var(--mk-space-2xl);
    }

    pre {
      margin-top: var(--mk-space-md);
      padding: 12px 14px;
      background: var(--mk-color-plate);
      border: var(--mk-rule-hair);
      border-left: var(--mk-rule-thick);
      color: var(--mk-color-heading);
      font-family: var(--mk-font-typewriter);
      font-size: var(--mk-size-mono-sm);
      line-height: 1.6;
      overflow-x: auto;
    }

    code {
      font-family: var(--mk-font-typewriter);
      font-size: 0.86em;
      background: var(--mk-color-plate);
      border: var(--mk-rule-hair);
      color: var(--mk-color-heading);
      padding: 1px 5px 0;
    }

    pre code {
      background: none;
      border: 0;
      padding: 0;
      font-size: inherit;
    }
  </style>
</Base>
